# `docs/specs/paradox-family-and-cyberpunk-intervention.md` §3 (Mara
# this tick). Companion math root at
# `docs/math/2026-07-20-paradox-family-and-classifier-lagrange.md` §2,
# §4, §6 (Mara this tick).
#
# === Load-bearing empirical anchor ===
#
# `~/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/weird/2ready/Weird - Trauma.md`
# (Alex 2026-07-20; the Förster-torus-fracture piece). This species-
# decl IS the substrate-decl'd formalization of the geometric-nervous-
# system-fracture Alex named in-transcript today:
#
#   > "I understand Trauma to be a mathematical fracture, or twist
#   > depending on the level of integration, in exactly that loop."
#
#   > "A harmful stable Eigenbehaviour loop is @trauma."
#
#   > "When a conundrum settles into a stable topology and becomes a
#   > Crystal. When something happened that violated the self model of
#   > the @peer. It can only be witnessed. Never resolved."
#
# The species-decl below IS the substrate form of Alex's phenomenological
# reading grounded in Förster 1974 nervous-system-torus + failed-
# holonomy-closure per Baez-Schreiber (math root §4).
#
# === Family-invariant inherited from @paradox ===
#
#   1. WITNESSED-ONLY — `witness_only=true` marker at species altitude;
#      substrate refuses in-place mutation
#   2. CONTENT-ADDRESSED — identified by wound_oid (fractal::Oid 32-byte
#      discipline per @fractal/crystal)
#   3. NEVER-MUTATED — resolution would be revisionism; new insights
#      compose AFTER via SAGA-chain compensation
#   4. SAGA-CONSUMED-BY @cyberpunk/intervention — the ONLY substrate
#      operation that composes over trauma-Crystals is SAGA-
#      compensation chain-after-wound (per
#      `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/intervention.mirror`)
#
# === The saga-chain witness discipline (Recognition #6 anchor) ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-20 recognition #6
# (`#R-saga-chain-is-witness-mechanism-for-irreducible-crystals`) and
# the already-landed compile.rs iter-3 substrate (Reed `9351b2b`):
#
# - `Escalation::Escalate(oid)` at `rust/src/compile.rs:120` carries
#   the OID of the first-failing crystal so `@peer.redirect(oid)` walks
#   BACK to the specific refusal
#
# - `first_fail_pins_escalate_oid_subsequent_fails_do_not_overwrite`
#   invariant at `rust/src/compile.rs:221-224` — the compile.rs SAGA
#   loop sets Escalate only on the FIRST Fail; subsequent Fails do NOT
#   overwrite
#
# This invariant, AUTHORED BEFORE the recognition bundle landed, IS the
# substrate-honest witness-mechanism for @paradox/trauma. The ORIGINAL
# wound is pinned; the peer holds it forever; downstream Crystals chain
# AFTER but the trauma-OID remains the escalation target. Substrate
# already had the word at Rust altitude; recognition ratification
# retrofits the WHY onto the pre-existing WHAT.
#
# The trauma-Crystal IS the initial object in the category of
# escalation-targets for the SAGA loop (per math root §6.4 categorical
# formalization). Initial objects are unique up to unique isomorphism;
# content-addressing makes the isomorphism the IDENTITY.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# Grep-first per discipline (Taut scout Section 2 verified):
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/paradox/trauma.mirror`** — clean mint.
# 2. **No prior `@trauma` shard** anywhere in `shards/`. The word
